---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CaptureForm from "../../components/forms/capture-form.astro";
const seo = { page_description: "Definition of FlateDecode compression in PDFs." };
---
<Layout title="What is FlateDecode?" seo={seo}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 py-16 prose">
    <h1>FlateDecode (Compression)</h1>
    <p><strong>Definition:</strong> FlateDecode is a standard compression filter used in PDF files. It is based on the zlib/deflate compression algorithm, which is the same technology used in standard ZIP files.</p>

    <h2>How it is Used</h2>
    <p>In a PDF, almost all <a href="/reference/topic-17">Content Streams</a> (the text and drawing instructions) and many images (like PNGs) are compressed using FlateDecode to save space. Without it, PDF files would be massive text documents.</p>

    <h2>Interaction with Tools</h2>
    <p>When you use an <a href="/tools/annotate-pdf">online annotation tool</a>, the tool must <em>decode</em> the streams to render the page, allow you to add annotations, and then optionally re-encode the data when saving. This is why a file might change size slightly after saving, even if you only added one small note. Check expected sizes with our <a href="/calculators/calc-1">File Size Estimator</a>.</p>

    <div class="mt-12 not-prose p-6 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold mb-4">Suggest an edit to this term</h3>
      <CaptureForm formLabel="feedback" submitText="Send Suggestion" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
